{"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Attributes","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Attributes","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","title":"MXLPrint.Attributes","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLPrintV10AttributesV","extendedModule":"IvorMXL","roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlprint\/attributes-swift.struct"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPrint"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"The print-attributes group is used by the print element. The new-system and new-page attributes indicate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whether to force a system or page break, or to force the current music onto the same system or page as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"preceding music. Normally this is the first music data within a measure. If used in multi-part music, they","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"should be placed in the same positions within each part, or the results are undefined. The page-number","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute sets the number of a new page; it is ignored if new-page is not “yes”. Version 2.0 adds a blank-page","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute. This is a positive integer value that specifies the number of blank pages to insert before the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"current measure. It is ignored if new-page is not “yes”. These blank pages have no music, but may have text or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"images specified by the credit element. This is used to allow a combination of pages that are all text, or all","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"text and images, together with pages of music.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPrint\/Attributes-swift.struct\/init(staffSpacing:startsNewSystem:startsNewPage:blankPage:pageNumber:)"],"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPrint\/Attributes-swift.struct\/blankPage","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPrint\/Attributes-swift.struct\/pageNumber","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPrint\/Attributes-swift.struct\/staffSpacing","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPrint\/Attributes-swift.struct\/startsNewPage","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPrint\/Attributes-swift.struct\/startsNewSystem"],"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPrint\/Attributes-swift.struct\/Equatable-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPrint\/Attributes-swift.struct","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Attributes","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The staff-spacing attribute specifies spacing between multiple staves in tenths of staff space. This is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deprecat